  "authoringNote": "Partial S3 snapshot (D5 absent target). Only f13x6-order v2 is supplied; its metadata supersedes {f13x6-order, 1}, which is not in the snapshot. C08 checks kind and subject only between supplied endpoints, so there is no integrity rejection, no applied edge and no invented target: the superseded list is empty and no superseded reference appears anywhere. v2 is a valid final order naming the case subject and the receipt links it. R01 to R05 pass on v2 with the standard citation sets (8, 6, 9, 6, 4). R09 passes. R06 is manual_review for the qualified_clinical_reviewer with R06.clinical_review (no refs, effect none) and cites the five /clinical/ statements of the usable encounter; R07 passes citing /lcmpReport/incorporated (false; the null evaluationDate is not cited); R08 passes; R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. Every parent is empty; both lists are empty. State ready_for_review. Recorded reading: a rule cites evidence-field facts only from the documents it reads, and R04 reads only final current usable records; every usable encounter and order here is final, so no draft is excluded. The standard chronology holds: the order date 2026-09-08 is after the 2026-08-24 encounter (not the same day, so C02 does not apply) and inside the C01 bound 2027-02-24, and the receipt at 2026-09-09T16:30:00Z is after the C06 span of the order date, which ends 2026-09-09T12:00Z. Deferred to S4: the kind and subject checks repeat when v1 arrives; arrival-order recovery, history display, replay, rollback prevention and human acceptance are not exercised.",
